# id: M56-term-gated-only-on-what-is-dirty-now
# covering-test: TestATermStaysGatedAfterALaterMarkClosesEmpty
# package: ./raft/
# expect: killed
# power-seeds: 60
# power-floor: 30
# power-ceiling: 5
# power-measured: 59 of 60, first at seed 0, under current at A6's close -- and 280 of 300 in a four-shard run where every shard's FIRST seed detects. The clean tree is 0 of 300. It is caught by persist-before-reply with the plainest verdict in the repository: node 2 sent a vote-resp advertising term 1 while only term 0 was durable. THE PREVIOUS DECLARATION WAS AN OPT-OUT AND IT WAS FALSE: it read 'the same schedule M53 needs, and unreachable for the same measured reason', which is reasoning by ANALOGY -- it cited M53's measurement and never took its own. M53 needs an empty mark to exist -- it swaps closeEmptyMark for releaseThrough on one -- and this replaces m := r.hsMark with PersistMark(0) in raft/raft.go, which ungates the term whenever hardStateDirty is false, which is most of the time, and needs no rare interleaving at all. And it was false ON THE DAY IT WAS WRITTEN rather than gone stale: re-measured under POWER_CONFIG=a5, the shape it was written against at commit 7a809a4, it is 28 of 30 first at seed 0 against a clean tree at 0 of 30. It stood because scripts/power-mutants.sh SKIPS any patch carrying a power: line, so an opt-out exempts itself from the only instrument that could refute it (DESIGN-A6 section 42.3). Floored at half the measured rate; the ceiling is 5 rather than a multiple of the first detecting seed, because that seed is 0
# mutates: a message revealing this node's term is gated on what is dirty NOW rather than on the mark the hard state was handed over under. The two differ exactly when a mark stops being current without becoming durable -- a later mark closing empty -- and the term's durability goes with it (BUG-017, second half)
--- a/raft/raft.go
+++ b/raft/raft.go
@@ -2430,7 +2430,7 @@
 // the term, and gating the term on it would make the term's constraint
 // disappear the moment that unrelated mark was satisfied.
 func (r *Raft) termMark() PersistMark {
-	m := r.hsMark
+	m := PersistMark(0)
 	if r.hardStateDirty && r.dirtyMark > m {
 		m = r.dirtyMark
 	}
